  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Unsettled weather expected Sunday through Wednesday\nas a front remains stalled over the region...temperatures \ntrending cooler by Wednesday.\n\nStalled front to our south will return as a warm front Sunday,\nonly to clash with another southward moving upper level trough \nMonday and Tuesday. A wholesale uptick in rain chances are\nexpected for both Monday and Tuesday. 48 hour probabilistic \nensemble guidance indicates 80 percent chance for 0.50, 50% \nchance of 1.00 and 25% chance of 1.50 or more. This is good \nnews since we are in need of the rain. \n\nBy Wednesday the upper trough digs in from the northwest while \nthe front shifts southeast. Cooler air from the north with high \npressure wedge will have our highs Wednesday running 10 to 15 \ndegrees below normal, followed by a gradual return to near\nnormal temperatures by the weekend.",
